<title>USA: French finmin told G7 about cutting workweek.</title>
<headline>French finmin told G7 about cutting workweek.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn was asked to explain at G7 talks on Friday how the new Socialist-led government planned to carry out its promise to cut the working week without loss of pay, European Commissioner Yves-Thibault de Silguy said.</p>
<p>De Silguy told reporters that Strauss-Kahn had told finance ministers from the Group of Seven countries meeting on Friday night that the cut in the working week would help boost demand.</p>
<p>&quot;The Americans were a bit doubtful,&quot; de Silguy said after talks between economic ministers from the United States, Canada, Japan, Britain, France, Italy and Germany, plus the European Commission.</p>
<p>The talks were held as part of the summit of G7 leaders here.</p>
</text>
